  "prompt_text": "The figure is a schematic of a CD8+ T cell showing how its phenotype and function are shifted toward stronger anti-tumor cytotoxic T lymphocyte activity. In the center, the cell is linked to changes in transcriptional regulators, with T-BET, EOMES, and ID3 increased and NFAT reduced, suggesting a reprogrammed internal state.\n\nAround the membrane, several visible changes point to enhanced killing capacity: higher expression or activity of effector molecules such as GZMB, IFNγ, TNF, and FASL, together with lower levels of inhibitory or exhaustion-associated receptors including PD1, TIM3, BTLA, and LAG3. Other receptors, including IL-12R and IL-2Rα, appear associated with improved responsiveness to cytokines and are tied to enhanced effector differentiation and survival.\n\nThe diagram also emphasizes broader functional consequences. On one side, CX3CR1, CXCR4, and MMPs are associated with greater migration and invasive potential. Elsewhere, arrows indicate clonal expansion, enhanced memory CTL differentiation, and altered metabolism. Taken together, the figure presents a coordinated program in which CD8+ T cells become more proliferative, longer-lived, less inhibited, and more cytotoxic.",
